,"organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"If we're making stuff `thread_local` anyway, do we even need this new `flushing` variable?\r\n\r\n`flush_read_ptr` will only ever be accessed/modified from a single thread at a time, and it's always reset to zero before the mutex is unlocked, so it's effectively already `thread_local` in a sense.\r\n\r\nMaking it actually `thread_local` would mean that we could move the `MutexLock` back to where it was before #112506 (after the reentrancy check) and the recursive flushing would work like it used to, without this extra stuff.","created_at":"2025-12-09T14:19:42Z","updated_at":"2025-12-09T14:20:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113802#discussion_r2602872859","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113802","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2602872859"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113802#discussion_r2602872859"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113802"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2602872859/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":110,"original_line":110,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2603075505","pull_request_review_id":3557968663,"id":2603075505,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6bJ8ex","diff_hunk":"@@ -157,10 +158,19 @@ class CommandQueueMT {\n \t}\n \n \tvoid _flush() {\n+\t\t// Safeguard against trying to re-lock the binary mutex.\n+\t\tif (flushing) {\n+\t\t\treturn;\n+\t\t}\n+\n+\t\tflushing = true;\n+\n \t\tMutexLock lock(mutex);\n \n \t\tif (unlikely(flush_read_ptr)) {\n-\t\t\t// Re-entrant call.\n+\t\t\t// Another thread is flushing.\n+\t\t\tlock.temp_unlock(); // Not really temp.\n+\t\t\tsync();","path":"core/templates/command_queue_mt.h","commit_id":"824287eefb3de4ebe62857c2e24c18b3d18bd89e","original_commit_id":"73805445e8838125378a025ba25934032325b36b","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Indeed! Fixed.","created_at":"2025-12-09T15:09:46Z","updated_at":"2025-12-09T15:09:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113802#discussion_r2603075505","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113802","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2603075505"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113802#discussion_r2603075505"},"pull_request":{"href":"http