,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6bM-af","diff_hunk":"@@ -157,10 +158,20 @@ class CommandQueueMT {\n \t}\n \n \tvoid _flush() {\n+\t\t// Safeguard against trying to re-lock the binary mutex.\n+\t\tif (flushing) {\n+\t\t\treturn;\n+\t\t}\n+\n+\t\tflushing = true;\n+\n \t\tMutexLock lock(mutex);\n \n \t\tif (unlikely(flush_read_ptr)) {","path":"core/templates/command_queue_mt.h","commit_id":"824287eefb3de4ebe62857c2e24c18b3d18bd89e","original_commit_id":"824287eefb3de4ebe62857c2e24c18b3d18bd89e","user":{"login":"brycehutchings","id":5100250,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDAyNTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5100250?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings","html_url":"https://github.com/brycehutchings","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Is this check needed at all? When I look at how `flush_read_ptr` interacts with the mutex, it looks like it is always set to 0 before the mutex is released. So any time we get past the mutex being acquired, isn't `flush_read_ptr` guaranteed to be 0? It seems like it should just flow down to the while loop and run that normally.\r\n\r\nThis check used to be before the mutex acquire, and there it made sense to avoid the deadlock issue (although it had race condition problems). By moving it to after the mutex, the deadlock issue was introduced, but now the condition should never happen. At least I think so?","created_at":"2025-12-09T18:37:28Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T16:09:32Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113802#discussion_r2603869855","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113802","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2603869855"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113802#discussion_r2603869855"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113802"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2603869855/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":170,"original_line":170,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":23,"position":23,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2607364901","pull_request_review_id":3563437918,"id":2607364901,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6baTsl","diff_hunk":"@@ -157,10 +158,20 @@ class CommandQueueMT {\n \t}\n \n \tvoid _flush() {\n+\t\t// Safeguard against trying to re-lock the binary mutex.\n+\t\tif (flushing) {\n+\t\t\treturn;\n+\t\t}\n+\n+\t\tflushing = true;\n+\n \t\tMutexLock lock(mutex);\n \n \t\tif (unlikely(flush_read_ptr)) {","path":"core/templates/command_queue_mt.h","commit_id":"824287eefb3de4ebe62857c2e24c18b3d18bd89e","original_commit_id":"824287eefb3de4ebe62857c2e24c18b3d18bd89e","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.